{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CebKnyimFxKw9q6ZajNSj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three tasks are complete and committed on `feature/pair_transparency-in-search`. Summary of what happened:\n\n- **TASK-1 & TASK-2**: Restyled both `libraries/shared/Search.svelte` and `contacts/Search.svelte` inputs to use the same tinted/blurred surface as `UiNotifications` (`bg-c-neutral/60 ... backdrop-blur-sm ... dark:bg-s-dark/80`).\n- **TASK-3 (verification)**: Booted the app in a temporary preview route and screenshotted it — discovered the plain class change alone rendered fully opaque due to a pre-existing global rule in `src/styles/components/forms.css` that sets an *unlayered* `background-color` on all inputs, which under CSS Cascade Layers always beats a `@layer`'d Tailwind utility regardless of specificity. Fixed by marking just these two inputs' background utilities `!important`, without touching the global forms.css (which every other input in the app relies on). Re-verified with screenshots in light and dark mode confirming the frosted-glass effect now works and typed text stays legible.\n\nOne pre-existing, out-of-scope issue was noted in `implementation.md`: in dark mode, both search inputs (and the `UiNotifications` reference itself) show low-contrast dark text because neither sets an explicit `dark:text-*` class — confirmed identical on the reference component, so not a regression from this fix, just flagged for awareness.\n\nThe worktree is clean and everything is committed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_read_input_tokens":112087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":551},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b1fa74e-133f-